  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-13> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-13--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-13--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch12-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.51" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.505"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The assertion can be made exact for individual models, but its unrestricted scope and informal cost comparison prevent a single decisive test. Existing programs permit counterexample searches and special-case proofs, while general computational lower bounds are difficult and cannot be inferred from simulation alone." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Define irreducibility for a specified system family as a lower bound on algorithms predicting state at time t relative to direct evolution, then prove the bound or search for faster predictors. A predictor with asymptotically fewer steps refutes the claim for that family; a valid lower-bound proof confirms it there." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "No single formal definition of \"almost as many\" applies across all systems.", "Finite simulation cannot establish an asymptotic lower bound.", "General prediction questions can be undecidable." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-13--gpt--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch12-13--gpt--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
